    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d231">

                <pb facs="0465" n="403" sameAs="frus:frus1944Quebec/pg403"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">J.C.S.
                    Files</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Note by the Secretaries of the Combined Chiefs of
                        Staff</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        C.C.S. 618/4</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quebec</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-09-12">12 September 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Machinery for Coordination of
                        United States-Soviet-British Military Effort</hi></p>
                <p>In accordance with the instructions of the Combined Chiefs of Staff in the C.C.S. 172d Meeting,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d231-f1"
                    /> the Secretaries propose that the British Chiefs of Staff and the United
                    States Chiefs of Staff send the messages attached hereto as Enclosures “A” and
                    “B” to Generals Burrows and Deane respectively.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d231-f2"
                    /></p>
                <closer><signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. J. McFarland</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. T. Cornwall-Jones</hi>
                    </signed><lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Combined Secretariat</hi></closer>



                <xi:include href="d231-a1.xml" xpointer="d231-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d231-a2.xml" xpointer="d231-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d231-f1" n="1" xml:id="d231-f1-content">
                <p>See <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg308">p. 308</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d231-f2" n="2" xml:id="d231-f2-content">
                <p>At their 173d Meeting, September 13, 1944, the Combined Chiefs of Staff agreed to
                    the dispatch of the enclosed messages to Burrows and Deane. See <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg320">p. 320</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
